  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Issued in a square wooden box. Consists of sixty-four small black and white books arranged to resemble a chess board. The text in each book indicates which chess piece the book represents.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="546" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Rules in English and German.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="520" ind1="8" ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">96 miniature books (each 40 x 40 mm.) issued in covered wooden box. 48 vol. are of black paper, printed in white; 48 vol. are of white paper, printed in black. When 32 v. of each color are arranged in a grid, alternating colors so as to form a chessboard, a game of chess may be played with the 32 v. that remain. Each vol. contains one of 32 literary quotations that reveals its function as a chess piece (pawn, castle (for rook), horse (for knight), bishop, queen, king). With an insert ([2] leaves on 1 folded sheet ; 15 x 6 cm.) giving the title, the artist's name and the year "1984," and instructions for playing.</subfield>
  </datafield>
